<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Rectangle ABCD, with <m>A({2},\,{2})</m>, <m>B({5},\,{2})</m>, <m>C({5},\,{4})</m> and <m>D({2},\,{4})</m>, is mapped onto <m>A'B'C'D'</m>, with <m>A'({\frac{1}{2}},\,{2})</m>, <m>B'({\frac{7}{2}},\,{2})</m>, <m>C'({2},\,{4})</m> and <m>D'({-1},\,{4})</m>, by a shear. Mwangi describes the shear. One step has a mistake.</p><ol><li>Points on the x-axis do not move, so the x-axis is invariant.</li><li>Corner C moves <m>{4}</m> units in the negative x-direction.</li><li>C is <m>{4}</m> units from the x-axis.</li><li>Shear factor = <m>{-1}</m>.</li><li>Matrix = <m>{\left[\begin{array}{cc} 1 &amp; -1 \\ 0 &amp; 1 \end{array}\right]}</m>.</li></ol><p>(a) Which step has the mistake?</p><div>[ Step 1 | Step 2 | Step 3 | Step 4 | Step 5 ]  </div><p>(b) Give the correct shear factor.</p><div><fillin characters="5" name="ans2"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) The mistake is in Step 2. C moves from <m>C({5},\,{4})</m> to <m>C'({2},\,{4})</m>, which is <m>{3}</m> units, not <m>{4}</m>.</p><p>(b) Shear factor = <m>{-3} \div {4} = {-\frac{3}{4}}</m>, and the matrix is <m>{\left[\begin{array}{cc} 1 &amp; -\frac{3}{4} \\ 0 &amp; 1 \end{array}\right]}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p>Step 2</p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>-\frac{3}{4}</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>